BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:stimuleringsfonds-grounding-the-cloud-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260830T101526Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260914
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260915
SUMMARY:Deadline: Stimuleringsfonds: Open Call Grounding the Cloud 2026
DESCRIPTION:Open call from the Creative Industries Fund NL (Stimuleringsfon
 ds) for projects within digital culture that provide insight into and redu
 ce the ecological impact of digital technology. Data storage in the cloud\
 , generative AI chatbots and other everyday digital habits carry major eco
 logical consequences: the energy consumption of data centres\, the raw mat
 erials used for hardware\, and ever-growing e-waste. The Fund encourages p
 rojects that make the ecological (and therefore also social) impact of dig
 ital technologies and data consumption tangible\, question it\, and put al
 ternative working methods into practice\, around topics such as regenerati
 ve culture\, degrowth\, low-tech\, the reuse of obsolete hardware\, and re
 sponsibility for the technologies we use within digital culture. Applicati
 ons may concern new projects or the reinterpretation or further developmen
 t of existing initiatives that show scope for more depth or a changed appr
 oach. Collaborations in which designers\, makers or researchers engage wit
 h sustainability from an intersectional perspective are explicitly encoura
 ged. The grant may be used for artistic and substantive development\, rese
 arch\, collaboration\, knowledge sharing\, presentation and documentation.
  ELIGIBILITY: individual makers\, designers\, researchers or collectives w
 orking on alternative ways of handling digital technology\, registered wit
 h a Chamber of Commerce within the Kingdom of the Netherlands. Grant award
 s a maximum of EUR 30\,000\; maximum project duration one year. This call 
 is open from 17 August 2026\, 15:00 CEST until 14 September 2026\, 16:00 C
 EST. No application fee. Questions: digitalecultuur@stimuleringsfonds.nl.\
 n\nOrganisation: Stimuleringsfonds Creatieve Industrie (Creative Industrie
 s Fund NL)\nLocation: Netherlands. Requires Dutch Chamber of Commerce (KvK
 ) registration within the Kingdom of the Netherlands.\nAward: Maximum EUR 
 30\,000 per grant. No application fee.\nDuration: Project-based\; maximum 
 project duration one year.\n\nMore: https://www.stimuleringsfonds.nl/en/gr
 ants/open-call-grounding-the-cloud?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&u
 tm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.stimuleringsfonds.nl/en/grants/open-call-grounding-the-clou
 d?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Netherlands. Requires Dutch Chamber of Commerce (KvK) registration
  within the Kingdom of the Netherlands.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:stimuleringsfonds-immerse-interact-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260830T101526Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260825
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260826
SUMMARY:Deadline: Stimuleringsfonds + Film Fund: Immerse\\Interact 2026 (se
 cond round)
DESCRIPTION:Immerse\\Interact is a joint grant scheme of the Stimuleringsfo
 nds Creatieve Industrie and the Netherlands Film Fund for immersive and in
 teractive media projects (VR\, MR\, AR and other interactive storytelling)
 . It supports artistic projects with a supporting cinematic component\, in
  which fiction or non-fiction storytelling in relation to interactive (web
 -based/mobile) or immersive technologies (XR\, room-scale projections) is 
 central. It funds both development and realisation. Development support is
  EUR 15\,000 for individual makers (plus up to EUR 5\,000 coaching\, cappe
 d at EUR 20\,000 total) or EUR 25\,000 for producers (plus up to EUR 5\,00
 0 coaching)\; the coaching contribution requires a motivation from both ap
 plicant and coach plus the coach's CV\, and the development phase must res
 ult in a usable prototype. A maximum of six development contributions are 
 awarded per round\, to keep the development and realisation budgets in bal
 ance. Realisation support is up to EUR 35\,000 for individual makers or up
  to EUR 125\,000 for producers (the Fund covers a maximum of 85 percent of
  the production budget)\; note that at realisation stage the producer may 
 not also be the director\, screenwriter or designer. A separate Presentati
 on Procedure offers presentation grants for projects previously supported 
 by Immerse\\Interact after 1 January 2022. EUR 600\,000 is available per F
 und in 2026. Open to professional makers\, collectives and producers with 
 a demonstrable track record in immersive or interactive media\; applicants
  must be registered with the Dutch Chamber of Commerce (KvK). The second 2
 026 round runs 24 June to 25 August 2026 (opens 24 June 15:00\, closes 25 
 August 16:00 CEST). No application fee. Questions: immerseinteract@stimule
 ringsfonds.nl.\n\nOrganisation: Stimuleringsfonds Creatieve Industrie and 
 the Netherlands Film Fund\nLocation: Netherlands. Requires Dutch Chamber o
 f Commerce (KvK) registration.\nAward: Development: EUR 15\,000 for indivi
 dual makers (plus up to EUR 5\,000 coaching\, max EUR 20\,000) or EUR 25\,
 000 for producers (plus up to EUR 5\,000 coaching). Realisation: up to EUR
  35\,000 for individual makers or up to EUR 125\,000 for producers (Fund c
 overs max 85 percent). No application fee.\nDuration: Project-based\, deve
 lopment and realisation phases.\n\nMore: https://www.stimuleringsfonds.nl/
 en/grants/immerse-interact-grant-scheme?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantd
 esk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.stimuleringsfonds.nl/en/grants/immerse-interact-grant-schem
 e?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Netherlands. Requires Dutch Chamber of Commerce (KvK) registration
 .
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:stimuleringsfonds-international-vouchers-2026@artificialnouveau.github.
 io
DTSTAMP:20260830T101526Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261027
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261028
SUMMARY:Deadline: International Vouchers
DESCRIPTION:Travel voucher for Dutch-based professionals in design\, archit
 ecture and/or digital culture who have been invited by a foreign party to 
 give a presentation\, lecture or workshop. To apply you must have submitte
 d an application to the Fund in the past five years that was positively as
 sessed (previous International Vouchers do not count). The inviting foreig
 n party must cover a proportionate share of the costs. Covers hourly fees\
 , travel and accommodation directly related to the activity. IMPORTANT TIM
 ING RULE: applications are accepted from 5 months to a minimum of 7 weeks 
 before the activity begins\, and processing takes about 6 weeks. This lead
  time can rule out activities that fall shortly after a round opens. Round
  2 (4 May to 22 June 2026) has closed. Round 3 runs 8 September 2026 15:00
  CEST to 27 October 2026 16:00 CEST\, with a budget of EUR 33\,000\; given
  the 7-week rule it effectively serves activities starting from late Octob
 er 2026 onwards. IMPORTANT PREREQUISITE: you must already have had an appl
 ication to the Fund positively assessed within the past five years\, and a
  previous voucher does not satisfy this\, so this is not a viable first ap
 proach to the Fund. The window runs 8 September 2026\, 15:00 CEST to 27 Oc
 tober 2026\, but closes early once 20 complete applications are received. 
 Maximum one voucher per applicant per calendar year.\n\nOrganisation: Stim
 uleringsfonds Creatieve Industrie (Creative Industries Fund NL)\nLocation:
  Netherlands (for international travel)\nAward: Up to €1\,500 within Eur
 ope (zone 1) / up to €2\,500 outside Europe (zone 2)\nDuration: Per trip
 \n\nMore: https://www.stimuleringsfonds.nl/en/grants/international-voucher
 s?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.stimuleringsfonds.nl/en/grants/international-vouchers?utm_s
 ource=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Netherlands (for international travel)
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:rijkscultuurfondsen-interdisciplinary-grant-2026@artificialnouveau.gith
 ub.io
DTSTAMP:20260830T101526Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261001
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261002
SUMMARY:Deadline: Rijkscultuurfondsen: Interdisciplinary Grant
DESCRIPTION:The Interdisciplinary grant is a new joint scheme of the six Du
 tch national cultural funds (Mondriaan Fund\, Performing Arts Fund NL\, Fu
 nd for Cultural Participation\, Netherlands Film Fund\, Creative Industrie
 s Fund NL\, and the Dutch Foundation for Literature)\, announced on 7 July
  2026. It supports makers and organisations whose work genuinely crosses t
 he boundaries of the individual funds' disciplines (visual art\, design\, 
 film\, literature\, performing arts\, and cultural participation) and cann
 ot be contained within a single discipline. TWO TRACKS: an Individual trac
 k for professional makers with a demonstrable interdisciplinary practice (
 at least one year of experience\; income cap EUR 55\,000 including the gra
 nt\; approximately EUR 24\,900 for 12 months)\; and an Organisation track 
 for organisations running multi-discipline projects. AMOUNT: EUR 12\,500 t
 o 50\,000 per project. ELIGIBILITY: makers and organisations based in the 
 Netherlands or the Caribbean part of the Kingdom. APPLYING: handled throug
 h the Mondriaan Fund's online application portal (info@mondriaanfonds.nl)\
 ; an account is required in advance. DEADLINE: 1 October 2026\, 16:00 Dutc
 h time (single application round).\n\nOrganisation: Dutch national cultura
 l funds (Rijkscultuurfondsen)\, via the Mondriaan Fund\nLocation: Netherla
 nds. For professional makers and organisations based in the Netherlands or
  the Caribbean part of the Kingdom whose practice spans multiple disciplin
 es.\nAward: EUR 12\,500 to 50\,000 per project. The individual-maker track
  is approximately EUR 24\,900 for 12 months (income cap EUR 55\,000 includ
 ing the grant).\nDuration: Up to 12 months for the individual-maker track.
 \n\nMore: https://www.mondriaanfonds.nl/en/apply-for-a-grant/grants/interd
 isciplinary/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.mondriaanfonds.nl/en/apply-for-a-grant/grants/interdiscipli
 nary/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Netherlands. For professional makers and organisations based in th
 e Netherlands or the Caribbean part of the Kingdom whose practice spans mu
 ltiple disciplines.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:waag-trust-me-im-an-airtist-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260830T101526Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260930
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261001
SUMMARY:Deadline: Trust me\, I'm an AI/rtist: Open Call for Creative Interv
 entions
DESCRIPTION:Waag Futurelab invites artists\, theatre makers\, choreographer
 s\, dancers\, game designers and other creative practitioners to engage di
 rectly with seven experimental generative AI Enablers being co-created wit
 h technologists and dance\, theatre and gaming professionals. The call is 
 an invitation into the development process: selected artists get access to
  the technologies\, datasets\, interfaces and assumptions that shape these
  systems while they are still being built. Rather than testing whether the
  systems work\, artists are asked to interrogate why they work the way the
 y do\, who they are designed for\, what forms of creativity they enable or
  constrain\, and what assumptions about culture\, intelligence\, authorshi
 p\, labour\, bodies\, audiences and society are embedded in them. Waag is 
 looking for individuals and collectives willing to move beyond adoption in
 to investigation\, and welcomes proposals that are speculative\, critical\
 , poetic\, provocative\, humorous\, performative\, constructive or disrupt
 ive\, including work that challenges\, misuses\, reimagines\, hacks\, subv
 erts or plays with the tools\, exposes hidden biases\, questions environme
 ntal costs\, or imagines alternative technological futures. THE SEVEN AI E
 NABLERS\, each requiring an on-site visit to its technology partner: the G
 eneric Procedural Content Generation Enabler (text-to-3D assets and avatar
 s\, CERTH\, Greece)\; the Data-Driven Cultural Content Adaptation Enabler 
 (audience-aware creative content ideation with ranked candidate ideas\, CE
 RTH\, Greece)\; the Cross-Domain Audience Engagement Analytics Enabler (tu
 rning heterogeneous cultural participation data into interpretable engagem
 ent signals\, The Audience Agency\, Warrington\, UK)\; the Dance Style Ana
 lysis and Generation Enabler (dance video into virtual 3D choreography\, d
 issected into body\, effort\, shape and space components\, Centre of Excel
 lence for Research & Innovation\, Cyprus)\; the Immersive Design Integrati
 on Enabler for Dance & Theatre (NLP-driven XR environments with speech-to-
 3D scene editing\, Cyprus)\; the Music-to-Movement Translation Enabler (au
 dio into a time-aligned feature set spanning genre classification\, emotio
 nal valence-arousal analysis\, rhythm extraction and latent-space projecti
 on\, feeding motion generation\, spatial audio and visual choreography\, A
 ristotle University of Thessaloniki\, Greece)\; and the Adaptive Narrative
  Enabler for Games & Theatre (an evolutionary AI trained on creator-writte
 n story elements that generates infinite story variations\, explicitly rej
 ecting LLMs because of their dependence on copyrighted or public-domain co
 rpora that encode 19th and early 20th century sexism\, racism and imperial
 ism\, CAUSA Creation\, Austria). ELIGIBILITY: artists\, designers\, creati
 ve technologists\, theatre makers\, dancers\, choreographers and game desi
 gners\, as individuals or collectives\; applicants must hold a European VA
 T number. An info session with live demonstrations of the AI Enablers runs
  31 July 2026\, 10:00 to 11:30 CEST (meeting ID 995 7016 2341). Applicatio
 ns go through Homerun using the official Application Template\, uploaded a
 s a PDF\; read the Guide for Applicants\, which contains the full Enabler 
 descriptions\, before applying. Questions: zoenie at waag dot org. The AI 
 Enablers and this call are part of the Horizon Europe project HAMLET\, whi
 ch aims to make generative AI accessible to cultural organisations of all 
 sizes. Closes 30 September 2026\, 23:59 CEST. Free to apply.\n\nOrganisati
 on: Waag Futurelab (Horizon Europe project HAMLET)\nLocation: Europe. Enga
 ging with a specific AI Enabler includes an on-site visit to its technolog
 y partner: CERTH (Greece)\, The Audience Agency (Warrington\, UK)\, the Ce
 ntre of Excellence for Research & Innovation (Cyprus)\, Aristotle Universi
 ty of Thessaloniki (Greece)\, or CAUSA Creation (Austria). Final presentat
 ions September 2027.\nAward: EUR 20\,000 commission fee excluding VAT\, in
 clusive of artist fee\, travel\, accommodation and production costs. Appli
 cants must have a VAT number in Europe. No application fee.\nDuration: Jan
 uary to September 2027\, with final presentations in September 2027\n\nMor
 e: https://waag.org/en/article/open-call-creative-interventions-trust-me-i
 m-airtist/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://waag.org/en/article/open-call-creative-interventions-trust-me-i
 m-airtist/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Europe. Engaging with a specific AI Enabler includes an on-site vi
 sit to its technology partner: CERTH (Greece)\, The Audience Agency (Warri
 ngton\, UK)\, the Centre of Excellence for Research & Innovation (Cyprus)\
 , Aristotle University of Thessaloniki (Greece)\, or CAUSA Creation (Austr
 ia). Final presentations September 2027.
END:VEVENT
END:VCALENDAR
